From uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com  Thu Mar 17 18:31:08 2016
From: uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com (Altuna Akalin)
Date: Thu, 17 Mar 2016 18:31:08 +0000
Subject: Re: [methylkit_discussion] Error in methylation calling, sorting and legitimate Bismark SAM file
Message-ID: <OoDWkCma4Bk.DvUklbD3AwAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <OoDWkCma4Bk.rFvecALyAwAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
References: <OoDWkCma4Bk.ELpTscuoAwAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com> <OoDWkCma4Bk.rFvecALyAwAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/OoDWkCma4Bk/m/DvUklbD3AwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

please make sure your sam file conforms to the example shown here:
https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/master/inst/extdata/test.fastq_bismark.sorted.min.sam

also described in the bismark manual
http://www.bioinformatics.babraham.ac.uk/projects/bismark/Bismark_User_Guide.pdf

your columns are scrambled and the script can not find the methylation call string from bismark where it should be. In addition, you have too few reads to call methylation. This could be because of the way you subsampled. There are no overlapping reads, you won't be able to get reliable methylation calls out of this even if you fix the issue with the file format.

Best,
Altuna

